257
00:17:08,440 --> 00:17:10,760
Oh, hey, come on now, Hermes.

258
00:17:12,180 --> 00:17:13,217
How you feeling?

259
00:17:13,300 --> 00:17:14,829
I'm just a little curious.

260
00:17:16,680 --> 00:17:17,917
I really want to know,

261
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:21,457
how did it feel to get revenge on the
son of a bitch who murdered your sister?

262
00:17:21,540 --> 00:17:24,317
Did you get some sort of sick
satisfaction out of burring

263
00:17:24,400 --> 00:17:27,694
me alive in that sewer pipe
you called an improv coffin?

264
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:30,640
It's Sports Maximum!

265
00:17:32,580 --> 00:17:34,320
Hey, what's going on, Hermes?

266
00:17:34,460 --> 00:17:36,107
What are you doing up there?

267
00:17:36,940 --> 00:17:38,020
Sorry, Jolene!

268
00:17:39,800 --> 00:17:43,397
The ground has a long memory of
everything that happens upon it.

269
00:17:43,480 --> 00:17:47,520
Sort of like a tape recorder, or
even much like a digital camera.

270
00:17:48,020 --> 00:17:48,860
For example,

271
00:17:49,080 --> 00:17:51,317
it remembers that boy who was shot dead by

272
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:53,737
his own father when he
fell onto the ground.

273
00:17:53,820 --> 00:17:55,457
Shit, where the hell are you?

274
00:17:55,540 --> 00:17:57,717
It even remembers the
gangster who was buried

275
00:17:57,800 --> 00:18:00,037
alive in a sewer pipe
and drowned to death.

276
00:18:00,120 --> 00:18:04,097
The Earth's memory is so powerful that it
can even recall every single one of the

277
00:18:04,180 --> 00:18:09,062
passengers who met their demise on a plane
that fell to the ground in July of 2005,

278
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:10,160
six years ago.

279
00:18:10,680 --> 00:18:11,510
Hermes, hey!

280
00:18:11,740 --> 00:18:13,497
What the hell are you doing up there?

281
00:18:13,580 --> 00:18:16,680
Come on, Hermes! Stop! Let go of me!

282
00:18:17,580 --> 00:18:19,737
I'm here thanks to Versus Standability.

283
00:18:19,820 --> 00:18:20,650
See,

284
00:18:20,733 --> 00:18:22,317
Netherworld uncovers all
the folks who met the ground

285
00:18:22,400 --> 00:18:25,224
when they perished and
excavates their memories.

286
00:18:40,900 --> 00:18:42,040
Excuse me, ladies.

287
00:18:42,420 --> 00:18:43,302
Welcome aboard.

288
00:18:43,660 --> 00:18:44,490
Unfortunately,

289
00:18:44,573 --> 00:18:46,437
this plane is expected
to lose control and crash

290
00:18:46,520 --> 00:18:50,980
into the ground at approximately
21.33 on July 21st, 2005.

291
00:18:51,540 --> 00:18:55,097
We ask that you please turn off
all electronic devices and make

292
00:18:55,180 --> 00:18:59,239
sure that your seatbelt is securely
fastened around your lower waist.

293
00:19:00,120 --> 00:19:01,937
I suggest you heed that warning,

294
00:19:02,020 --> 00:19:06,020
or you'll end up like the man who
was sitting in the seat behind me.

295
00:19:07,020 --> 00:19:10,255
His head was lodged straight
into my stomach on impact.

296
00:19:10,560 --> 00:19:12,900
What? Ain't no way. Damn it!

297
00:19:13,080 --> 00:19:14,315
Where's the entrance?

298
00:19:14,460 --> 00:19:15,557
Start looking, Hermes!

299
00:19:15,640 --> 00:19:16,581
Help me find it!

300
00:19:16,800 --> 00:19:18,640
Wait, what even is this place?

301
00:19:18,880 --> 00:19:20,717
Is this a hallucination, Jolene?

302
00:19:20,800 --> 00:19:22,237
It should be on the ceiling!

303
00:19:22,320 --> 00:19:24,379
Look for the place we came in from!

304
00:19:24,760 --> 00:19:27,157
Everything in this fucking
plane feels so real, though!

305
00:19:27,240 --> 00:19:28,837
We need to find the way out of here, now!

306
00:19:28,920 --> 00:19:32,297
Before you fell down, was there anyone
coming to check the room above the hall?

307
00:19:32,380 --> 00:19:35,397
There was a panic in the halls
after that boy's dad was shot.

308
00:19:35,480 --> 00:19:37,277
The police had to have shown up.

309
00:19:37,360 --> 00:19:38,520
Did you see anyone?

310
00:19:38,760 --> 00:19:40,880
No, I have no clue. Besides,

311
00:19:41,120 --> 00:19:43,457
even if the cops came, they
wouldn't be able to hear us calling,

312
00:19:43,540 --> 00:19:45,897
just like I couldn't hear
you up there earlier.

313
00:19:45,980 --> 00:19:47,377
How's this plane down here anyway?

314
00:19:47,460 --> 00:19:52,166
I didn't see anything like this when I
was waiting for you to come out the hall.

315
00:19:53,980 --> 00:19:54,921
Excuse me, miss.

316
00:19:55,080 --> 00:19:56,537
Please refrain from punching the ceiling.

317
00:19:56,620 --> 00:19:59,738
If you would, kindly take
your seat and wait quietly.

318
00:20:00,620 --> 00:20:03,855
This plane will be crashing
in less than three minutes.

319
00:20:05,180 --> 00:20:07,120
Okay, then let us see the pilot!

320
00:20:07,360 --> 00:20:09,577
We gotta make him land
this plane immediately!

321
00:20:09,660 --> 00:20:12,425
Now hurry up, lady, and
take us to the cockpit!

322
00:20:12,820 --> 00:20:13,700
No point.

323
00:20:18,820 --> 00:20:21,232
We weren't able to land the plane safely.

324
00:20:21,900 --> 00:20:23,841
That's the reason why we crashed.

325
00:20:24,720 --> 00:20:25,680
Holy shit!

326
00:20:27,440 --> 00:20:30,087
Unfortunately for us,
we all burned to death.

327
00:20:30,400 --> 00:20:33,760
When the plane crash landed, it exploded.

328
00:20:34,060 --> 00:20:36,340
And that was when my body...

329
00:20:37,620 --> 00:20:39,360
Um, excuse me, sir.

330
00:20:39,620 --> 00:20:41,477
Did you not hear me
when I told everyone to

331
00:20:41,560 --> 00:20:44,442
turn off all of their
electronic devices earlier?

332
00:20:44,840 --> 00:20:45,700
Could it be?

333
00:20:46,140 --> 00:20:47,800
I think I remember this.

334
00:20:47,960 --> 00:20:50,380
It was flight number 2882 to Dallas.

335
00:20:50,680 --> 00:20:53,897
Around six or seven years ago, it
crashed somewhere near Orlando.

336
00:20:53,980 --> 00:20:55,617
We're dealing with ghosts here.

337
00:20:55,700 --> 00:20:58,400
No, we're memories. That's all.

338
00:20:58,580 --> 00:21:01,517
Remnants of memories that
were recorded by the Earth.

339
00:21:01,600 --> 00:21:05,541
Are you trying to tell me we're
actually gonna crash in this thing?

340
00:21:09,820 --> 00:21:12,900
Can you not make this plane
crash happen any faster?

341
00:21:13,600 --> 00:21:17,541
I've been sensing weather forecasts
getting closer to our position.

342
00:21:25,700 --> 00:21:29,297
It appears that he is drawing
ever closer toward this hospital.

343
00:21:29,380 --> 00:21:34,740
I swear to God, if you don't shut the fuck
up already and stop confusing me. Huh.

344
00:21:35,240 --> 00:21:36,652
Were you speaking to me?

345
00:21:41,740 --> 00:21:45,387
Netherworld's ability is to
excavate memories from the ground.

346
00:21:45,560 --> 00:21:51,140
And this plane is set to crash
specifically at 2133 on the dot. Also,

347
00:21:51,340 --> 00:21:53,257
try not to forget that
I've capitalized on this

348
00:21:53,340 --> 00:21:56,811
opportunity and managed to pull
Urmas into my hole as well.

349
00:21:58,200 --> 00:22:00,376
I have done this all for you, Father.

350
00:22:01,240 --> 00:22:03,040
Now just leave it to me.

351
00:22:26,320 --> 00:22:30,200
Although you think I cope

352
00:22:31,820 --> 00:22:35,400
My head is filled with hope

353
00:22:36,820 --> 00:22:43,800
Of some place other than here

354
00:22:46,540 --> 00:22:50,200
Although you think I smile

355
00:22:51,820 --> 00:22:55,400
Inside and all the while

356
00:22:57,080 --> 00:23:03,440
I'm wondering About my destiny

357
00:23:05,980 --> 00:23:09,080
I'm thinking about

358
00:23:11,880 --> 00:23:14,600
All the things

359
00:23:16,780 --> 00:23:19,480
I'd like to do

360
00:23:25,960 --> 00:23:29,277
I'm a dreamer,

361
00:23:29,360 --> 00:23:34,397
a distant dreamer,

362
00:23:34,480 --> 00:23:38,177
dreaming far

363
00:23:38,260 --> 00:23:44,540
away from today.

364
00:23:50,720 --> 00:23:52,120
Thank you.

365
00:24:19,980 --> 00:24:22,300
Thank you.
